  "summary": "Malicious code in ded-pwa-bnpl-forms-test-demo (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package downloads and executes a second-stage binary. It fingerprints the OS/architecture and fetches a platform-specific payload over HTTPS from oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, and /pkg/package.exe, with a DNS-TXT base64 fallback channel via the *.dl[.]wel1[.]ru domain family (c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru). The downloaded payload is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt; (or dotnet_diag_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt;.exe under the Windows temp dir), made executable, and launched as a detached background process (cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows, /bin/sh -c '... \u0026' on Unix).",
